rtest tour, by Held–Karp dynamic programming (Bellman, “Dynamic programming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"treatment of the travelling salesman problem”, Journal of the ACM 9, 1962; Held and Karp,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“A dynamic programming approach to sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"code":"HeldKarpTSP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/graph\/shortesttour(weight:)","title":"shortestTour(weight:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shortestTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV","text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kin